Annexation – UDC-13-00071 – Swan Ranch II Annexation
Staff Report
July 2, 2013
Page 9

1) “An annexation of the area is for the protection of the health, safety and welfare of the
persons residing in the area and in the city or town.” Findings:   In order to meet this
criteria, the need for fire protection should be addressed. Without a new fire station in the
vicinity, emergency response will take longer than the standard set for the City and may
pull resources away from the rest of the City. Discussions between staff and the
developer regarding dedication of Lot 18, Block 2, Swan Ranch Rail Park, Eighth Filing,
for a future fire station at the corner of Clear Creek Parkway and the Wallick Road, but
the developer has not committed to such a dedication. In addition to land for the fire
station, the City must determine how to fund its construction, equipment, and staffing.
2) “The urban development of the area sought to be annexed would constitute a natural,
geographical, economical and social part of the annexing city or town.” Findings: The
property is approximately 8.7% contiguous to the existing City boundary. The site is
located within the PlanCheyenne comprehensive plan area and planned for urban services
expansion. The City has been gradually growing toward the subject property over the past
few years. People who work in this area likely reside, shop, and recreate in Cheyenne
facilities. The annexation area takes advantage of existing major facilities in the area
including major transportation corridors being proximate to the interchange of I-80 and I-
25.
3) “The area sought to be annexed is a logical and feasible addition to the annexing city or
town and the extension of basic and other services customarily available to the residents
of the city or town shall, within reason, be available to the area proposed to be annexed.”
Findings:  The area sought to be annexed is planned for urban services expansion in
numerous City planning documents including PlanCheyenne, which is the Cheyenne
Area comprehensive plan and the Board of Public Utilities master plan. The City’s water
and sewer system has capacity to serve this area and construction has begun on a major
water transmission line through the annexation area which is planned to be complete in
2014. Providers of City services have reviewed the proposed annexation and the
annexation area, which is predominately undeveloped, and have determined that the area
can be served within reason by City facilities and resources. Future development of the
area may require additional facilities and resources. As mentioned, City Fire service to
the area needs to be addressed. The need for other public facilities should also be
evaluated in discussions on establishment of development impact fees.
4) “The area sought to be annexed is contiguous with or adjacent to the annexing city or
town, or the area meets the requirements of W.S. § 15-1-407.” Findings:  The property is
approximately 8.7% contiguous with existing City limits.
5) “If the city or town does not own or operate its own electric utility, its governing body is
prepared to issue one (1) or more franchises as necessary to serve the annexed area
pursuant to W.S. § 15-1-410.” Findings:  Franchises are in place to serve this property.
6) “The annexing city or town, not less than twenty (20) business days prior to the public
hearing required by W.S 15-1-405(a), has sent by certified mail to all landowners and
affected public utilities within the territory a summary of the proposed annexation report
as required under subsection (c) of this section and notice of the time, date and location
of the public hearing required by W.S. § 15-1-405(a).” Findings:  The required
information was sent March 25, 2013.
