March 8, 2010 and a
Development Agreement with the City of Cheyenne April 22, 2011. The Board of Public
Utilities (BOPU) supports any City Annexation or BOPU Outside Users Agreements. The Sawn
Ranch Rail Park currently has BOPU’ Sewer and Non-Potable water from a well that feeds into a
water tank. This water supply is designate for fire protection only. These User’s in the Swan
Ranch Rail Park must enter into a Outside Users Agreements with the BOPU. Any User that
wants to use the Non-Potable water for use the restroom of their facility must also enter into a
Memorandum of Understanding between the BOPU and Swan Ranch Properties, LLC. Currently
Granite Peak Development is planning this spring to construct a 12” water main and 10” sewer
main in the Swan Ranch II. This construction will began at the intersection of Berwick Dr. and
Tundra Dr., run east along Berwick Dr. to Wallick Rd. turn south down Wallick Rd to Clear
Creek Parkway. The BOPU is schedule to have completed in June of 2014, a 42” water main
ready to be release for service. This 42” water is coming from the north and will run south down
Berwick RD. to Granite Peak Dr., turn southeast on Granite Peak Dr  and run down to Clear
Creek Parkway, turn south and run down Quartz Dr., turn southeast run under the interstate to
the east.
Before any business can hooks to the water and sewer they must hire Wyoming Professional
Engineer to submit a proposed site plans with all utilities and overall projected design, plans and
profiles to the Board of Public Utilities. After BOPU’s review and signature of approval, the
design engineer will need to send the plans to the (D.E.Q.) for approval and a permit to
construct. When the D.E.Q. permit is issued, City’s Engineer’s Office and Cheyenne Fire
Department have reviewed and signatures of approval are obtained. Then the Agent/Owner may
employ a licensed contractor to install the utilities, apply for all applications for water/sewer tap
permits from the BOPU, and request a preconstruction meeting with all parties involved prior to
construction.
All water and sanitary sewer utilities need to be designed and constructed in accordance with the
latest City of Cheyenne and Board of Public Utilities Construction Specifications Standards and
Standard Drawings and the latest Rules & Regulations for Establishing Policies & Design
Criteria of the Board of Public Utilities Cheyenne, Wyoming.
